{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>You shall surely strike him down.</b> The words of the Torah are wholly compassion from the Master of compassion, exalted be He; and when He commands us to put to death one who is liable, the intent is not that we do so by way of vengeance, to take revenge upon him because he incurred the liability — for that would be a cause to habituate our nature in the trait of cruelty — but the intent in His vengeance is by way of compassion, to have compassion upon the rest. Hence He mentioned before it, ״ולא תחוס עינך עליו״ — and your eye shall not spare him — and after it, ״וכל ישראל ישמעו וייראון ולא יוסיפו לעשות כדבר הזה עוד״ — and all Israel shall hear and fear and shall not again do such a thing — ״ובערת הרע מקרבך״ — and you shall burn the evil from your midst — ״וכל ישראל ישמעו וייראו״ — and all Israel shall hear and fear."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:07.036196658Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}